== The Economy — Farming Without Grinding

"Grind" is what it feels like when you do not know the economy. Learn the loops and the game funds itself.

=== Zenny & Points Loops

- *Zenny:* quest rewards + selling surplus parts. The classic pitfall is never selling because "I might need it" — sell what the smithy does not currently use; the game marks materials needed for a selected craft.
- *Kamura Points:* gathering, subquests, and special rewards. Spent at meal tickets, buddy gear, and trading — treat points as a second wallet, not a hoard.
- *Meowcenaries:* keep expeditions running at all times — they are passive material income with zero effort.
- *Argosy:* configure the trade routes toward whatever the smithy currently needs. It turns "I need three more of this" into "it arrives by itself."

=== Endemic Life: The Free Buffs

Spiribirds are the visible ones — collect the color-coded birds on your route for health/stamina/attack/defense. But the ecosystem has more:

- *Toads and environmental traps* — every map has explosive toads, vines, and falls; a monster lured into one is a free knockdown.
- *Stinkmink-style lures* — some endemic life drags monsters to you or away; use them to control the fight's location.
- Make a *route*: grab birds and useful endemic life on the way to the monster every single hunt. It is free power and free control.

=== Material Farming, Deliberately

1. Check the Hunter's Notes: which monster, which part, which break/carve/capture method drops what.
2. Target the *fastest* source, not the most reliable: capture quests are fast, part breaks are targeted, and some materials only come from specific breaks.
3. Run *subquests* and event quests that pay the material you need as a bonus.
4. If a material only drops from a painful fight, that fight is your training target — farming *is* practice.

=== MR Material Loops

Master Rank materials follow the same rules but multiply the layers: afflicted materials (from clusters), anomaly materials (Part 5), and follower-quest rewards. Keep the passive loops (Meowcenaries, Argosy) pointed at MR materials and the smithy stays stocked without dedicated farming sessions.

#tip[
  The best anti-grind tool is *variety*: alternate between your target farm and a different monster every few hunts. The game quietly funnels everything you need into the smithy from every direction — as long as you keep playing, the economy keeps feeding you.
]
